  "literary_context": "The references combine apocalyptic vision, a Gospel sign and its aftermath, apostolic proclamation, extended argument, pastoral reassurance, and visions of judgment and renewal. John 20 narrates encounters with the risen Jesus; 1 Corinthians 15 argues for resurrection and describes its transformed character. Their different forms show both narrated events and the meaning later texts draw from them.",
  "covenantal_significance": "Paul grounds future resurrection in God’s raising of Jesus, and the cited letters use this hope to address faithful life and grief. Revelation links resurrection hope with judgment and the removal of death in the renewed creation. These passages present resurrection as more than survival after death: they speak of God raising the dead and renewing life.",
